                                        "entry_id": "d1e00dac-a1e8-341d-a919-67b1a7a00934",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Having much learning, knowledgeable, erudite; highly educated."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "bc014192-0f35-484b-b15c-252aa2f66a17",
                                                "sense_id": "521e4556-d937-3229-b83d-36ac1083901f",
                                                "text": "the learned Merlin, well could tell, / Vnder what coast of heauen the man did dwell […]"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "ce52e486-fbb5-40b9-9677-52f137bfe460",
                                                "sense_id": "521e4556-d937-3229-b83d-36ac1083901f",
                                                "text": "My learned Brother Cresswell directed the jury to make the calculation […]"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "bad43791-2315-4464-84bd-200db4dc2cad",
                                                "sense_id": "521e4556-d937-3229-b83d-36ac1083901f",
                                                "text": "The book opens with the Time Traveler dining with learned peers in late 1800s England, where he is trying to convince them that he has invented a time machine."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "ee94649e-c3e9-4cc1-b5ac-4ac14828d8e4",
                                                "sense_id": "521e4556-d937-3229-b83d-36ac1083901f",
                                                "text": "HENRY WADSWORTH LONGFELLOW used to be both the best-known poet in the English-speaking world and the most beloved, adored by the learned and the lowly ..."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "efa7210d-d042-32f4-82b7-959749f83406",
                                        "entry_id": "d1e00dac-a1e8-341d-a919-67b1a7a00934",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A courteous description used in various ways to refer to lawyers or judges."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "formal"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": []
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "cda9e1ea-0938-37fb-a92a-db5b6bfb4f10",
                                        "entry_id": "d1e00dac-a1e8-341d-a919-67b1a7a00934",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Scholarly, exhibiting scholarship."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "04f32efb-2ea1-40b7-bee3-c811d9af77a3",
                                                "sense_id": "cda9e1ea-0938-37fb-a92a-db5b6bfb4f10",
                                                "text": "But our limits will not permit us to discuss the many important and curious questions respecting the science of government, to which this learned work invites attention."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
